Turnip's darwin backend over the guest's virtio GPU: Droid-VM/UniXNU wip/droidvm patches/mesa/turnip-darwin-virtgpu.patch, ported to
this build's Mesa (its memory-pressure hunk left out: this backend has no such watch). With TU_DARWIN_VIRTGPU=1 (or the kernel's
DROIDVM_VIRTGPU_PARAM_DEFAULT_3D) every NativeAdreno ABI method is served by a DRM native context of the virtio GPU (DroidVMVirtgpuABI.h:
NativeAdreno's methods 0x7200 on, open type 0x4149, served by DroidVMDisplay's DroidVMVirtioGpu3D.cpp) instead of the KGSL proxy. The
accelerator is the class TU_DARWIN_SERVICE names (macOS: AGXAccelerator, which the Metal plugin sets), else the iOS IOAcceleratorES.

